# Copy to ".env.local" in the repo root (gitignored) for local build configuration.
# Account provider buttons in this tree are local preview labels only; no OAuth client IDs are consumed.
#
# Local dev is fixed to http://localhost:5173 (vite.config.ts strictPort). Free that port if `npm run dev` fails.
# Optional: absolute deploy origin (no trailing slash) so Open Graph / Twitter preview images use full URLs at build time.
# VITE_PUBLIC_ORIGIN=https://your-app.vercel.app

# Public HTTPS URL to hosted privacy-policy.html (Chrome Web Store + Welcome / Settings links).
# VITE_PRIVACY_POLICY_URL=https://your-org.github.io/brandops/privacy-policy.html

# Membership demo gate: off by default and supported only during local development.
# This repo has no Stripe callback/webhook or verified entitlement service.
# VITE_ENFORCE_MEMBERSHIP_GATE=1
# Optional static billing navigation links. Opening one does not activate membership.
# VITE_STRIPE_CHECKOUT_URL=https://buy.stripe.com/...
# VITE_STRIPE_BILLING_PORTAL_URL=https://billing.stripe.com/p/session/...
#
# Skip the local preview identity wall (direct to Chat/workspace).
# VITE_SKIP_LAUNCH_AUTH=1

# --- Intelligence rules (optional) ---
# Default: same-origin `/brandops-intelligence-rules.json` copied from `public/` at build time.
# Override with any HTTPS JSON URL that returns a partial rules pack (see `public/brandops-intelligence-rules.example.json`).
# VITE_INTELLIGENCE_RULES_URL=https://your-cdn.example/brandops-intelligence-rules.json

# --- Hosted NLP (OpenAI-compatible) ---
# 401/403 from the inference URL almost always mean API key or model access — see Settings → AI bridge and worker model IDs.

# --- Optional webhook bridge proxy (local/server process, not bundled into the extension) ---
# These process variables are not loaded from .env.local automatically. Export them in the shell or
# inject them with your process manager/service configuration before `npm run bridge:proxy`.
# BRIDGE_PROXY_PORT=8787
# BRIDGE_SHARED_SECRET=replace-with-a-long-random-secret
# BRIDGE_TARGET_URL=https://your-hosted-receiver.example/agent-bridge
# BRIDGE_UPSTREAM_TIMEOUT_MS=10000
# Fixed-window inbound rate limit, keyed by client IP. Off unless set to 1.
# BRIDGE_RATE_LIMIT=1
# BRIDGE_RATE_LIMIT_WINDOW_MS=60000
# BRIDGE_RATE_LIMIT_MAX=60
# Local verification only: enables POST /agent-bridge on the bridge proxy itself.
# Production should leave this unset and use a real hosted receiver above.
# BRIDGE_ENABLE_LOCAL_RECEIVER=1
# Each provider POST route fails closed unless its authenticity secret is configured.
# The deployed receiver must have the same BRIDGE_SHARED_SECRET from its own trusted configuration;
# the secret is never included in the forwarded JSON body.
# TELEGRAM_WEBHOOK_TOKEN=replace-with-the-token-configured-on-your-telegram-webhook
# WHATSAPP_VERIFY_TOKEN=replace-with-the-GET-subscription-challenge-token
# WHATSAPP_APP_SECRET=replace-with-the-Meta-app-secret-used-to-sign-POST-bytes

# --- RevenueCat (mobile purchases) -------------------------------------------
# Public SDK keys from the RevenueCat dashboard, one per platform. These are
# public by design: RevenueCat client keys are safe to ship, and the entitlement
# is verified against the App Store / Play Store rather than trusted from here.
#
# Absent means purchasing is UNAVAILABLE, not free. `entitlements.ts` reports
# `not-configured`, `isPremium` stays false, and the paywall says purchases
# cannot be completed in this build instead of offering a button that dead-ends.
#
# There is no key for web: RevenueCat's Capacitor SDK is native-only, so a web
# build reports `no-native-purchases`.
#
# Also required before a purchase can succeed, and none of it lives in this file:
#   - a "pro" entitlement in the RevenueCat dashboard (see PREMIUM_ENTITLEMENT_ID)
#   - products and an offering attached to it
#   - matching products in App Store Connect / Play Console
# VITE_REVENUECAT_IOS_KEY=appl_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# VITE_REVENUECAT_ANDROID_KEY=goog_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
